 in 2013 she was arrested for DUI  again when she reportedly parked her car  on california's i 5 freeway blocking the  lane traffic she was also arrested for  some violent crimes she was charged with  corporal injury upon a spouse in March  2012 and that November both she and her  husband Robert Joseph Gilliam were  arrested after an alleged domestic  disturbance Kelly's battle with  addiction didn't end well she died  shortly after checking into rehab in  August 2013 the Los Angeles County  Coroner deem that her death was due to  combined drug intoxication in an  the dental overdose she was 43 John  Ritter was a staple of American TV for  decades best known as Jack Tripper on  the long-running sitcom Three's Company  he didn't slow down after that show  where its spin-offs ended in the late  80s he helped coin the term dramedy with  the ABC show Cooperman in the early 90s  he led the political satire hearts of  fire a senatorial aide John Hartman he  also had memorable film appearances like  1996 oscar-winning Slingblade  Ritter's final role was protective  father Paul Hennessy on the ABC sitcom 8  simple rules in September 2013 while  rehearsing for the show he was taken to  the hospital after vomiting and  complaining of chest pains initially he  was treated for a heart attack but it  was later discovered that he had a tear  in his aorta  he died during surgery a week shy of his  55th birthday wasn't supposed to happen  mom not now when we were old and gray  and living someplace warm  Shelley Morrison enjoyed a long fruitful  acting career including regular  appearances as sister see snow on the  Sally Field starring 60s sitcom The  Flying Nun but the role she became best  known for wouldn't come until 1999 with  the season 1 finale Will &amp; Grace rosario  is mentioned as early as the series  premiere but we don't actually meet her  until the season 1 finale when karen  gets jacked to marry rosario so she  won't be deported rosario wasn't meant  to show up beyond that episode but she  proved to be popular enough to stick  around while she works as Karen's made  over the course of the series that's  eventually revealed that she has a  degree in clinical psychology performed  with Jennifer Lopez and somehow rakes in  three hundred and fifty thousand dollars  per year Morrison was asked to reprise  the role for the 2017 Will &amp; Grace  revival but by that point she had  retired from acting for good in December  2019 news broke that she had passed away  from heart failure after a brief illness  at the age of 83 Rosie and I would do  other normal couple things you know like  get into a fight at IKEA while he died  much too young Merlin Santana had a  decade's long career in sitcoms in the  early 90s he played the recurring role  of Stanley boyfriend of Rudy Huxtable on  The Cosby Show shortly after his  character Marcus proved to be one of the  most popular parts of getting by a  short-lived sitcom about two single  mothers and their children Merlin's last  big regular sick  spot was as young ladies man Romeo  Santana on The WB's The Steve Harvey  Show that show ended in 2002 the same  year that Santana was killed in his car  in Los Angeles he was only 26 years old  when he was shot in the head by a man  named Damien Andre gates who apparently  erroneously believed that Santana had  been making advances toward his  girlfriend Gates was sentenced to three  consecutive life sentences plus 70 years  in prison for killing Santana and for  attempting to kill fellow actor Brandon  Quinton Adams who was in the car with  Santana during home improvements eight  seasons one of the most popular  characters was also it's least visible  with his face always obscured usually by  offense Earl hyneman's Wilson W Wilson  jr. doled out Yoda like wisdom to the  tool obsessed Tim Taylor audiences  didn't get to see Wilson's entire face  until the series finales curtain call  though in the meantime the show  occasionally had fun with the audience  by showing the bottom half of his face  but not the top Heinemann had been  working in film and TV since the 60s  mainly in smaller roles his big screen  credits include the 1981 military school  drama taps and the 1985 westerns  Silverado before home improvement he was  best known as Detective lieutenant Bob  Reed on the soap opera Ryan's Hope four  years after home improvement ended the  man behind Wilson had to give another  goodbye in December 2003 Hindman died of  lung cancer at the age of 61 well it's  not the only thing he ever did Gary  Coleman will always be remembered for  the role of Arnold Jackson on Diff'rent  Strokes Arnold was the younger of two  Harlem born brothers taken in by  successful businessman Phillip Drummond  Todd bridges played Arnold's older  brother Willis the namesake of Coleman's  classic catchphrase Lewis Coleman dealt  with severe health issues his whole life  while he was adamant about not publicly  sharing specifics it is known that his  short stature was due to kidney disease  he underwent at least two kidney  transplants that were ultimately  unsuccessful a year before his passing  he had heart surgery after which he was  seriously ill with pneumonia while  nothing has been made officially public  it seems likely that one or more of  these issues ultimately led to Coleman's  death he passed away in 2010 after  falling down the stairs in his home and  hitting his head he'd suffered a number  of seizures in the preceding months and  it's believed that those seizures may  have been what caused the fall the  injury eventually led to a brain  hemorrhage from which he didn't recover  and while that story line is too  familiar a famous kid struggling to find  way as an adult only to die young each  time it's just as tragic years before  Will Smith was punching out aliens he  was better known as half of the hip-hop  duo DJ Jazzy Jeff and The Fresh Prince  that Fame helped him eventually bridge  the worlds of hip-hop and acting with  the NBC sitcom The Fresh Prince of  bel-air Smith played a fictionalized  version of himself who sent to live with  his aunt and uncle in the Los Angeles  neighborhood bel-air after a  confrontation with a violent gang over  the course of the series James Avery  would become one of the most well-loved  father figures on American TV as Smith's  Uncle Phil  besides Fresh Prince Avery was also  known for his exceptional voice work he  was the voice of shredder in the  original Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles  animated series and of James Rhodes aka  war machine in the 90s iron man cartoon  as for his live-action work he didn't  have too many huge roles besides Uncle  Phil in a 2007 interview with the New  York Film Academy he was candid about  missing out on the spotlight saying you  can either be a movie star or an actor  I'm an actor but I've done pretty good  Avery died in December 2013 due to  complications from open-heart surgery he  was 68 in the first four seasons of the  80s sitcom growing pains Andrew Koenig  played boner best friend - Kirk  Cameron's Mike Seaver his character left  the show in season four to drop out of  college and joined the Marine Corps  gained exacting work after growing pains  wasn't extensive though he had some  other memorable claims to fame it was  the son of Walter caning best known as  the original Chekov on Star Trek  Andrew Koenig also starred in one of the  most famous fan films of all time he  played the Joker and Batman dead end in  which the Dark Knight finds himself  facing the Xenomorphs from the alien  films as well as the ruthless hunters  from the predator franchise in the 90s  and 2000's candy became an outspoken  activist and gained notoriety in his  efforts to draw more attention to  China's support to the military  dictatorship ruling Burma in 2008 he was  arrested for interrupting Pasadena's  rose parade by blocking a float  advertising the Beijing Summer Olympics  and holding up a sign that said China  free Burma in February 2010 canings body  was found hanging from a tree in  Vancouver's Stanley Park his father  confirmed at a press conference that his  son had taken his own life he later  wrote on his website that Andrew died  after a long battle with depression and  urged other depression sufferers to  reach out for help  David Strickland's acting career was  tragically short in the 90s he had  popular recurring roles on the sitcom  sister-sister and mad about you in 1996  he was tapped for the part he'll forever  be known for young eager rock reporter  Todd on the Brooke shield starring  suddenly Susan behind the scenes  Strickland suffered from mental health  and substance abuse issues his suddenly  Susan co-star nestor carbonell told  People magazine in 1999 if he had an  episode where he fell off the wagon it  would be once every two months sometimes  once every six months he'd have a bad  episode and we'd all worry about it for  a night or two and it resurfaced as if  nothing had happened  it always resurfaced Strickland was  reportedly off his prescribed medication  and upset about much of his role in the  1999 rom-com forces of nature being left  on the cutting room floor when he and  Andy Dick flew to Las Vegas in March  1999 the pair reportedly bounced from  strip club to strip club partying hard  and on March 22nd Strickland was found  in his motel room Reid hanged himself  with a bedsheet the writers of suddenly  Susan decided to have art imitate life  in the season 3 finale Todd's co-workers  panic when he goes missing they tell  stories about him interspersed with  clips of out of character interviews  with a cast the episode ends with the  police calling to report his fate which  is left ambiguous if you or anyone you  know is having suicidal thoughts please  call the National Suicide Prevention  lifeline at 1-800 to 73 talk 8255

